# Go conventions

Module `orchestrator/backend`. Package limits are in `docs/tech/0003-backend.md`.

- `internal/cli` and `internal/httpapi` call `internal/app`. They do not run SQL or encode a second error shape.
- `internal/machine` does not call git, models, or HTTP. `internal/router` does not call a provider.
- Map sentinels only as the HTTP table in `docs/tech/0003-backend.md`. Middleware order is Host, CORS, body cap, bearer, handler.
- `execChild` takes an argv slice. Refuse `sh` and `bash`. Never run a model string in a shell.
- Do not log bodies, tokens, model keys, or `databaseUrl`.

```go
// BAD
exec.Command("bash", "-lc", toolArg)

// GOOD
execx.Command(ctx, []string{bin, arg}, scrubbedEnv)
```
